IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaa-incapacity`
IMPORT `gaa-qa`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 1990 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (gaa-qa.l4): every exported question, for
-- every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the three roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none:
-- the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error.
-- Each question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE and every later input
-- ASSUMEd. For the person (the baseline's seat), each question is also asked against the baseline export on the same
-- facts. Mirror cases ask the same facts from the donor and the attorney, the appointor and the enduring guardian, and
-- the patient and the person responsible. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text, never copied from
-- the output. The people are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked instrument` IS AN Instrument
ASSUME `an unasked power of attorney` IS AN AttorneyInstrument
ASSUME `an unasked kind of power` IS AN AttorneyKind
ASSUME `an unasked power of guardianship` IS A GuardianshipInstrument
ASSUME `an unasked decision` IS A PersonalDecision
ASSUME `an unasked form` IS A DirectiveForm
ASSUME `an unasked directive` IS A Directive
ASSUME `an unasked standing` IS A `How I stand to the patient`

`as the person` MEANS `I am planning for my own incapacity, or a guardian or administrator may be appointed for me`
`as the attorney` MEANS `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
`as the enduring guardian` MEANS `I am, or have been asked to be, someone's enduring guardian`
`as the partner, relative, carer or friend` MEANS `I am the partner, relative, carer or friend of someone who may need treatment decided for them`

-- A power of attorney in Form 1 that continues despite incapacity, witnessed by a justice of the peace and an adult
-- who is not a donee, accepted by the donee, no substitute (s 104).
GIVEN `paragraph 4` IS A DurationDeclared
GIVETH AN AttorneyInstrument
`a power of attorney declaring` MEANS AttorneyInstrument WITH
    `in the form or substantially in the form of Form 1` IS TRUE
    `what paragraph 4 declares` IS `paragraph 4`
    `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS 1
    `other witnesses aged 18 or more who are not a donee or substitute donee` IS 1
    `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every donee` IS TRUE
    `a substitute donee is appointed` IS FALSE
    `a Form 2 acceptance is executed by every substitute donee` IS FALSE

-- A power of guardianship in the Schedule 1 form, the appointor's signature witnessed by two justices, the acceptance by
-- a justice and either another adult or nobody else (s 110E).
GIVEN `other acceptance witnesses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A GuardianshipInstrument
`a power of guardianship with other acceptance witnesses` MEANS GuardianshipInstrument WITH
    `in the Schedule 1 form or substantially so` IS TRUE
    `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction` IS TRUE
    `my signature: witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS 2
    `my signature: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` IS 0
    `those witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's` IS TRUE
    `signed by every appointee to accept` IS TRUE
    `each acceptance: witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS 1
    `each acceptance: other adult witnesses who are not me, my signer or an appointee` IS `other acceptance witnesses`
    `those witnesses signed in the appointee's presence and each other's` IS TRUE

-- A directive in the prescribed form, signed and witnessed by two justices, with a number of treatment decisions (s 110Q).
GIVEN `decisions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Directive
`a directive with treatment decisions` MEANS Directive WITH
    `in the prescribed form or substantially so` IS TRUE
    `I was encouraged to seek legal or medical advice` IS FALSE
    `signed by me, or for me in my presence and at my direction` IS TRUE
    `witnesses authorised to take declarations` IS 2
    `other adult witnesses who are not me or my signer` IS 0
    `the witnesses signed in my presence, any signer's and each other's` IS TRUE
    `treatment decisions it contains` IS `decisions`

§§ `For the person planning for incapacity`

-- Born 15 June 1990: 35 on 14 June 2026, 36 on 15 June 2026.
#ASSERT `How old am I on this day` `as the person` 1990 6 15 2026 6 14 EQUALS `aged` 35
#ASSERT `How old am I on this day` `as the person` 1990 6 15 2026 6 15 EQUALS `aged` 36
#ASSERT `How old am I on this day` `as the person` 1990 6 15 2026 6 15 EQUALS `aged` (`How old am I` 1990 6 15 2026 6 15)
-- s 4(3): presumed capable until the contrary is proved to the Tribunal.
#ASSERT `Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs` `as the person` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I presumed capable of managing my own affairs` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I presumed capable` TRUE)
-- s 43: an adult who cannot look after their own health and safety and needs a guardian: now; at 17, from 18; at 16,
-- or where an enduring guardian already meets the need (s 4(4)): no.
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` `as the person` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you now`
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` `as the person` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, from your 18th birthday: the Tribunal may appoint a guardian for you, to take effect then`
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` `as the person` 16 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for you`
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` `as the person` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the Tribunal may not appoint a guardian for you`
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint a guardian for me` `as the person` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the guardianship answer for` (`Can a guardian be appointed for me` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 64: both limbs and no less restrictive means: yes; an enduring power of attorney meets the need: no.
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal appoint an administrator of my estate` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can an administrator be appointed for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- ss 104(1a), 110B, 110P: 18 and of full legal capacity.
#ASSERT `May I make this instrument` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` 18 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I make this instrument` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` 17 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I make this instrument` `as the person` `an advance health directive` 30 FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I make this instrument` `as the person` `an advance health directive` 30 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I make the instrument` `an advance health directive` 30 TRUE)
-- ss 104C, 110D: an appointee of 18 with full legal capacity; a directive appoints no-one.
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person under my instrument` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` 18 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person under my instrument` `as the person` `an enduring power of guardianship` 17 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person under my instrument` `as the person` `an advance health directive` 30 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I appoint this person under my instrument` `as the person` `an enduring power of guardianship` 30 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I appoint this person` `an enduring power of guardianship` 30 TRUE)
-- Revocation: a capable donor revokes; an administrator or the Tribunal; only the Tribunal; Part 9A is silent on the
-- appointor; a treatment decision goes on a change of mind.
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` TRUE `an unasked fact` EQUALS `you may revoke it yourself`
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `your administrator may revoke it, or the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only the Tribunal may revoke it`
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an enduring power of guardianship` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the Act gives the Tribunal power to revoke it and is silent on revocation by you`
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an advance health directive` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `a treatment decision in it is revoked if you change your mind`
#ASSERT `How can this instrument of mine be revoked` `as the person` `an enduring power of attorney` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the revocation answer for` (`How can my instrument be revoked` `an enduring power of attorney` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 104: valid as made at 40; not with both paragraphs of paragraph 4 left in; not if made at 17.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney valid` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of attorney declaring` `it continues despite my later incapacity`) 40 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney valid` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of attorney declaring` `both paragraphs are left in`) 40 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney valid` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of attorney declaring` `it continues despite my later incapacity`) 17 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney valid` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of attorney declaring` `it continues despite my later incapacity`) 40 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of attorney validly created` (`a power of attorney declaring` `it continues despite my later incapacity`) 40 TRUE)
-- ss 104(1)(b), 105, 106: a continuing power is in force; a springing one only with a s 106 declaration.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney in force now` `as the person` TRUE `a continuing power` `an unasked fact` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney in force now` `as the person` TRUE `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney in force now` `as the person` TRUE `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of attorney in force now` `as the person` TRUE `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of attorney in force` `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal declare that I lack legal capacity` `as the person` TRUE `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal declare that I lack legal capacity` `as the person` TRUE `a continuing power` `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can the Tribunal declare that I lack legal capacity` `as the person` TRUE `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the Tribunal declare I lack legal capacity` `a power that springs on a section 106 declaration` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Has my substitute attorney become my attorney yet` `as the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Has my substitute attorney become my attorney yet` `as the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Has my substitute attorney become my attorney yet` `as the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Has my substitute attorney become my attorney` FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records and accounts` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records and accounts` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS amount `What is the most my attorney can be fined for not keeping records`
-- s 107(1)(c), (2): while I am capable my attorney may renounce; while I am incapable, only after a s 109(2) order or
-- for a recognised interstate or foreign power.
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` `as the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my attorney renounce my enduring power of attorney` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May my attorney renounce` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `What happens to my power of attorney if an administrator is appointed` `as the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Tribunal must revoke or vary your power to remove the inconsistency`
#ASSERT `What happens to my power of attorney if an administrator is appointed` `as the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Tribunal may revoke or vary your power, and your attorney answers to your administrator`
#ASSERT `What happens to my power of attorney if an administrator is appointed` `as the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the administration answer for` (`What happens to my power if an administrator is appointed` FALSE)
-- s 110E: valid with the acceptance witnessed by a justice and another adult; not by a justice alone.
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of guardianship with other acceptance witnesses` 1) 40 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of guardianship with other acceptance witnesses` 0) 40 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my enduring power of guardianship valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a power of guardianship with other acceptance witnesses` 1) 40 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my enduring power of guardianship valid` (`a power of guardianship with other acceptance witnesses` 1) 40 TRUE)
-- ss 110F, 110G(3): only while I cannot make reasonable judgments about my person, and in any circumstances the power sets.
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian act for me at this time` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian act for me at this time` `as the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian act for me at this time` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian act for me at this time` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian act for me now` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 45: where I live, yes; selling my house or consenting to an abortion, no.
#ASSERT `Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` `where I live` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` `selling my house` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` `consenting to an abortion` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Could a plenary guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` `with whom I associate` EQUALS `yes if` (`Could a plenary guardian make this decision` `with whom I associate`)
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` TRUE `where I live` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` TRUE `making a will for me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` TRUE `where I live` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` TRUE `where I live` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my enduring guardian make this decision about me` `as the person` TRUE `where I live` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May my enduring guardian make this decision` `where I live` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must my joint enduring guardians all agree` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must my joint enduring guardians all agree` `as the person` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Must my joint enduring guardians agree`
#ASSERT `May my surviving joint enduring guardians act after a death` `as the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my surviving joint enduring guardians act after a death` `as the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my surviving joint enduring guardians act after a death` `as the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May my surviving joint enduring guardians act` TRUE)
-- regs 7, 9: the current form from 4 August 2022; the former form until 3 February 2023; another form never.
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `the current Schedule 2 form` 2022 8 4 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `the current Schedule 2 form` 2022 8 3 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` 2023 2 3 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `the Schedule 2 form of the former regulations` 2023 2 4 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `some other form` 2024 1 1 EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Was the form of my directive the prescribed form` `as the person` TRUE `the current Schedule 2 form` 2022 8 3 EQUALS `yes if` (`Was my directive form prescribed` `the current Schedule 2 form` 2022 8 3)
-- ss 110P, 110Q: valid with three treatment decisions, though not encouraged to seek advice (s 110Q(2)); not with none.
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a directive with treatment decisions` 3) 30 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a directive with treatment decisions` 0) 30 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my advance health directive valid under the Act` `as the person` TRUE (`a directive with treatment decisions` 3) 30 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my advance health directive valid` (`a directive with treatment decisions` 3) 30 TRUE)
-- s 110R: voluntary and understood, yes; coerced, no.
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine valid` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine valid` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine valid` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my treatment decision valid` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- ss 110S(6), 110T: a change of mind revokes, unless its only sign is a later enduring power of guardianship; the
-- revocation statement in a later directive revokes.
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine revoked` `as the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine revoked` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine revoked` `as the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this treatment decision of mine revoked` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my treatment decision revoked` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 110S: operates when I cannot judge, in the circumstances it specifies, unless unforeseen circumstances would change a
-- reasonable person's mind; unforeseen alone does not stop it.
#ASSERT `Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` `as the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this treatment decision of mine operate now` `as the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does my treatment decision operate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 110ZD(4): no partner, an adult child: a child; nobody: no relative on the list; a partner: the partner.
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative for treatment decisions` `as the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a child`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative for treatment decisions` `as the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no relative on the list in s 110ZD(4)`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative for treatment decisions` `as the person` TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the spouse or de facto partner`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative for treatment decisions` `as the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the nearest relative answer for` (`Who is my nearest relative` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 110ZD(3)(c), (6): a carer of 50 who is the primary provider, on a carer payment only: yes; 17: no; paid: no.
#ASSERT `Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer` `as the person` 50 TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer` `as the person` 17 TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer` `as the person` 50 TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my carer count as my unpaid primary carer` `as the person` 50 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my carer my unpaid primary carer` 50 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible for treatment` `as the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `your nearest relative who is close to you`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible for treatment` `as the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no person responsible`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible for treatment` `as the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `your unpaid primary carer`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible for treatment` `as the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the person responsible answer for` (`Who is my person responsible` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 110ZJ: in order -- myself, my directive, my enduring guardian, my guardian, my person responsible, no-one.
#ASSERT `Who decides whether I get the proposed treatment` `as the person` TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `you decide yourself`
#ASSERT `Who decides whether I get the proposed treatment` `as the person` FALSE TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `the treatment decision in your directive`
#ASSERT `Who decides whether I get the proposed treatment` `as the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `your enduring guardian`
